cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use pkinative in academic work or cite it in publications,
  please cite it using the metadata below.
title: "pkinative — Zero-dependency native PKI toolkit"
abstract: >-
  A zero-dependency, pure-TypeScript toolkit for public-key infrastructure
  data: a strict ITU-T X.690 DER decoder and encoder (BER on request) with
  CWE-tagged resource limits, RFC 7468 PEM, object identifiers, and complete
  RFC 5280 X.509 certificate parsing covering every standard extension. It
  runs unchanged on Node.js, browsers, Deno, Bun and Workers, never
  implements secret-dependent cryptography, and is held to the x509-limbo and
  Wycheproof corpora by a blocking conformance gate.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Nizoka"
    email: "hello@pdfnative.dev"
    website: "https://pdfnative.dev"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Nizoka/pkinative"
url: "https://github.com/Nizoka/pkinative"
license: MIT
version: 0.4.0
date-released: 2026-09-25
keywords:
  - pki
  - x509
  - asn1
  - der
  - pem
  - rfc5280
  - typescript
  - zero-dependency
  - secure-by-default
